<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">raise-spectre</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Raise Spectre</ansi> spell binds a tormented spirit into an anguished,
terrifying form that feeds on fear and suffering. Spectres are instruments
of psychological devastation, striking at the mind and spirit rather than
flesh. Only the remains of powerful beings can withstand this binding.

Spectres are terrifying entities that assault foes with conviction-based
attacks that target the spirit. Their presence alone can unmake the resolve
of lesser combatants.

The servant's power scales with your Charisma and manifestation skill, and
with the remains you raise it from. Part of it is drawn from the corpse, so
the same spell over better remains yields a better servant. A spectre sits
in the middle of the raised undead in what it asks of you to keep.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast raise-spectre [corpse]</ansi>     Animate nearby remains.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> Extended channel
<ansi fg="yellow">Corpse:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Requires powerful remains</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Nearby corpse or ground loot</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Cast Cost:   </ansi> Moderate, and paid only once
<ansi fg="yellow">Held Cost:   </ansi> Modest, for as long as you keep it
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Manifestation</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The spectre appears under your command and aids you in combat.
  - Once raised, the undead servant remains active as a companion.
  - Use the <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> command to evaluate a corpse's quality.
  - Raising costs conviction once. Keeping the servant sets conviction
    aside for as long as it walks with you, and that held share, not
    the casting price, is what limits how many you can field.
  - A mightier servant holds more of your will, and better remains
    make a mightier servant.
  - Skill in manifestation lowers what a companion holds, so practice
    buys you a larger following as well as a stronger one.
  - If your conviction is already spoken for, the raising is refused
    outright rather than leaving you weaker, and costs you nothing.

